{
  "dom_id": "step-q104505",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Make $k$ the subject of the equation $-2h=2m-3k.$",
  "worked_solution": "We need to isolate $k,$ so we will treat the other variables $h$ and $m$ as constants. We can use the addition and multiplication principles to solve for $k.$\n\nFirst, we add $3k$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2h & =2m-3k \\\\ -2h+3k & =2m-3k+3k \\\\ 3k-2h & =2m\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we add $2h$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3k-2h & =2m \\\\ 3k-2h+2h & =2m+2h \\\\ 3k & =2m+2h\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides by $3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3k & =2m+2h \\\\ \\frac{3k}{3} & =\\frac{2m+2h}{3} \\\\ k & =\\frac{2(m+h)}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
